[I] Daemon for communication with eBUS heating systems

[T] ebusd is a daemon for handling communication with eBUS devices connected
[T] to the 2-wire energy bus used by numerous heating systems. It connects
[T] via serial, TCP or UDP adapters, decodes messages using configuration
[T] files and offers a TCP, HTTP and MQTT interface.

[U] https://github.com/john30/ebusd

[A] Ebusd Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] extra/base
[F] CROSS

[V] 26.1
[L] GPL3

